   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = - 3 x^{2} - x + 11 \\) and \\( g(x) = - x - 4 \\). The shaded region R shown is bounded by the graphs of f and g and the vertical lines \\( x = -2 \\) and \\( x = 2 \\). Find the exact area of R.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 44
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "On \\( [-2, 2] \\), \\( f(x) - g(x) = 15 - 3 x^{2} \\), which is positive, so f is the upper curve and the limits are the given vertical lines.",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99059",
         "rule_named": "upper minus lower"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{-2}^{2} \\left(15 - 3 x^{2}\\right)\\,dx \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "area between curves"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "An antiderivative of the integrand is \\( - x^{3} + 15 x \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99003",
         "rule_named": "power rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluating from \\( -2 \\) to \\( 2 \\), the area is \\( 44 \\).",
         "mathjson": 44,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"
      }
   ],
